node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store
.tade-test-*/
# Tade writes its own bookkeeping under .tade/ — task files, the context an
# agent was handed, pasted attachments, check runs, locks — and none of it is
# this project's: it is one machine's and one person's, and it was being
# committed. checks.yaml is the exception, because a person writes it, CI is
# generated from it and a test holds it to `pnpm check`.
#
# `/.tade/*` and not `/.tade/`: git does not descend into an ignored folder, so
# excluding the folder itself would take checks.yaml with it and the line below
# could never put it back.
#
# One of these earns its own note. `checks.running.json` says what is being
# checked right now and is taken back when the run ends, and while it is there
# `pnpm exec biome ci .` read it as a file somebody had written badly — which
# made `format` fail inside every run that wrote it.
/.tade/*
!/.tade/checks.yaml
